(MATHEMATICAL DERIVATION) Tj
50 509.0 Td
(========================) Tj
50 496.0 Td
(  Selection Sort comparisons = SUM\(i=0 to n-2\) \(n-1-i\)) Tj
50 483.0 Td
(                              = \(n-1\)+\(n-2\)+...+1 = n\(n-1\)/2) Tj
50 470.0 Td
() Tj
50 457.0 Td
(  Bubble Sort worst           = n\(n-1\)/2   [same sum]) Tj
50 444.0 Td
(  Insertion Sort worst        = SUM\(i=1 to n-1\) i = n\(n-1\)/2) Tj
50 431.0 Td
() Tj
50 418.0 Td
(  For n=1000: n\(n-1\)/2 = 499,500 comparisons \(confirmed by experiment\)) Tj
50 405.0 Td
() Tj
50 392.0 Td
() Tj
50 379.0 Td
(ENGINEERING RECOMMENDATION) Tj
50 366.0 Td
(===========================) Tj
50 353.0 Td
(  RECOMMENDATION: Use INSERTION SORT for the emergency dispatch system.) Tj
50 340.0 Td
() Tj
50 327.0 Td
(  Reasoning:) Tj
50 314.0 Td
(    1. Emergency data is typically NEARLY SORTED \(priority updates arrive) Tj
50 301.0 Td
(       incrementally, most items retain their relative order\).) Tj
50 288.0 Td
(    2. Insertion Sort achieves O\(n\) for sorted/nearly-sorted data.) Tj
50 275.0 Td
(    3. It is STABLE: equal-priority items retain their original order.) Tj
50 262.0 Td
(    4. It is ADAPTIVE: performance degrades gracefully with input disorder.) Tj
50 249.0 Td
(    5. Selection Sort is NEVER adaptive -- always O\(n^2\) -- avoid it here.) Tj
50 236.0 Td
(    6. For n > 10,000: upgrade to Merge Sort or Timsort \(O\(n log n\)\).) Tj
